From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:29:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 731/743] Read live activation rows in padded MXFP8 decode
 tiles

Base: candidate-40 source 5f926df6d3126266a9c88c82c06544060008c33c,
replayed from upstream 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354 plus
its ordered 574-patch series.

Rationale: padded activation and scale workspaces can contain unwritten
rows. Clamp inactive decode and split-K lanes to the final live row so
those consumer loads never depend on scratch contents outside live rows.

Quality: live rows retain their original inputs and accumulation order;
weights, quantization, token policy and output stores are unchanged.
Unused MMA lanes repeat a valid input. The changed copy lowering may
increase latency and must be measured before adoption.

Tests: canonical source replay, Python parsing and whitespace checks.
Adds odd/boundary cases, initially unwritten tails, then poisoned-tail
CUDA graph replay against an independent unpadded path. GPU compilation,
initcheck, memcheck, exact output and repeat timing remain unvalidated.

Upstream status: unsubmitted experimental prototype, not approved for
adoption. Hardware proof must precede an acceptance claim.
